{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you already created a project with the CLI or by cloning an example from the "},{"type":"link","href":"./getting-started","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Getting Started"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide, you can skip this guide and move on to the "},{"type":"link","href":"./guide/routing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Routing"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"So you want to build a TanStack Start project from scratch?"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This guide will help you build a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"very"}]},{"type":"text","value":" basic TanStack Start web application. Together, we will use TanStack Start to:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Serve an index page"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Display a counter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Increment the counter on the server and client"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://stackblitz.com/github/tanstack/router/tree/main/examples/react/start-counter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here is what that will look like"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let's create a new project directory and initialize it."}]},{"type":"code","value":"mkdir myApp\ncd myApp\nnpm init -y","lang":"shell"},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"We use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"npm"},{"type":"text","value":" in all of these examples, but you can use your package manager of choice instead."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typescript-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript Configuration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"We highly recommend using TypeScript with TanStack Start. Create a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsconfig.json"},{"type":"text","value":" file with at least the following settings:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"Bundler\",\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"strictNullChecks\": true\n  }\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enabling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"verbatimModuleSyntax"},{"type":"text","value":" can result in server bundles leaking into client bundles. It is recommended to keep this option disabled."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"install-dependencies","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install Dependencies"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start is powered by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/router","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and supports "},{"type":"link","href":"https://vite.dev/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vite"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"https://rsbuild.dev/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rsbuild"}]},{"type":"text","value":" as the build tool."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To install Start and Router, run:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm i @tanstack/react-start @tanstack/react-router","lang":"shell"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You'll also need React:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm i react react-dom","lang":"shell"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the build tool and React integration you want to use:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"npm i -D vite @vitejs/plugin-react","lang":"shell"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"npm i -D @rsbuild/core @rsbuild/plugin-react","lang":"shell"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"vite\",\"name\":\"vite\"},{\"slug\":\"rsbuild\",\"name\":\"rsbuild\"}]}","data-bundler-meta":"{\"bundlers\":[\"vite\",\"rsbuild\"]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you use Vite, you can also use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@vitejs/plugin-react-swc"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@vitejs/plugin-react"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"and some TypeScript:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm i -D typescript @types/react @types/react-dom @types/node","lang":"shell"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"update-configuration-files","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Update Configuration Files"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"We'll then update our "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package.json"},{"type":"text","value":" to use your build tool's CLI and set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"type\": \"module\""},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"{\n  // ...\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite dev\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\"\n  }\n}","lang":"json"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"{\n  // ...\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"rsbuild dev\",\n    \"build\": \"rsbuild build\"\n  }\n}","lang":"json"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"vite\",\"name\":\"vite\"},{\"slug\":\"rsbuild\",\"name\":\"rsbuild\"}]}","data-bundler-meta":"{\"bundlers\":[\"vite\",\"rsbuild\"]}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then configure TanStack Start's build tool plugin:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\nimport viteReact from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  server: {\n    port: 3000,\n  },\n  resolve: {\n    tsconfigPaths: true,\n  },\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart(),\n    // react's vite plugin must come after start's vite plugin\n    viteReact(),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"vite.config.ts\"","title":"vite.config.ts","file":"vite.config.ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { pluginReact } from '@rsbuild/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  server: {\n    port: 3000,\n  },\n  plugins: [pluginReact(), tanstackStart()],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"","title":"rsbuild.config.ts","file":"rsbuild.config.ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"vite\",\"name\":\"vite\"},{\"slug\":\"rsbuild\",\"name\":\"rsbuild\"}]}","data-bundler-meta":"{\"bundlers\":[\"vite\",\"rsbuild\"]}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"add-the-basic-templating","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add the Basic Templating"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are 2 required files for TanStack Start usage:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The router configuration"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The root of your application"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once configuration is done, we'll have a file tree that looks like the following:"}]},{"type":"code","value":".\n├── src/\n│   ├── routes/\n│   │   └── `__root.tsx`\n│   ├── `router.tsx`\n│   ├── `routeTree.gen.ts`\n├── `vite.config.ts` or `rsbuild.config.ts`\n├── `package.json`\n└── `tsconfig.json`"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-router-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Router Configuration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the file that will dictate the behavior of TanStack Router used within Start. Here, you can configure everything\nfrom the default "},{"type":"link","href":"/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/preloading","children":[{"type":"text","value":"preloading functionality"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"link","href":"/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/data-loading","children":[{"type":"text","value":"caching staleness"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You won't have a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"routeTree.gen.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" file yet. This file will be generated when you run TanStack Start for the first time."}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/router.tsx\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nexport function getRouter() {\n  const router = createRouter({\n    routeTree,\n    scrollRestoration: true,\n  })\n\n  return router\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-root-of-your-application","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Root of Your Application"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finally, we need to create the root of our application. This is the entry point for all other routes. The code in this file will wrap all other routes in the application."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/__root.tsx\nimport type { ReactNode } from 'react'\nimport {\n  Outlet,\n  createRootRoute,\n  HeadContent,\n  Scripts,\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  head: () => ({\n    meta: [\n      {\n        charSet: 'utf-8',\n      },\n      {\n        name: 'viewport',\n        content: 'width=device-width, initial-scale=1',\n      },\n      {\n        title: 'TanStack Start Starter',\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: RootComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RootComponent() {\n  return (\n    <RootDocument>\n      <Outlet />\n    </RootDocument>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction RootDocument({ children }: Readonly<{ children: ReactNode }>) {\n  return (\n    <html>\n      <head>\n        <HeadContent />\n      </head>\n      <body>\n        {children}\n        <Scripts />\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"writing-your-first-route","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Writing Your First Route"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now that we have the basic templating setup, we can write our first route. This is done by creating a new file in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/routes"},{"type":"text","value":" directory."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/index.tsx\nimport * as fs from 'node:fs'\nimport { createFileRoute, useRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nconst filePath = 'count.txt'\n\nasync function readCount() {\n  return parseInt(\n    await fs.promises.readFile(filePath, 'utf-8').catch(() => '0'),\n  )\n}\n\nconst getCount = createServerFn({\n  method: 'GET',\n}).handler(() => {\n  return readCount()\n})\n\nconst updateCount = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .validator((d: number) => d)\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const count = await readCount()\n    await fs.promises.writeFile(filePath, `${count + data}`)\n  })\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  component: Home,\n  loader: async () => await getCount(),\n})\n\nfunction Home() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const state = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      onClick={() => {\n        updateCount({ data: 1 }).then(() => {\n          router.invalidate()\n        })\n      }}\n    >\n      Add 1 to {state}?\n    </button>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That's it! 🤯 You've now set up a TanStack Start project and written your first route. 🎉"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can now run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"npm run dev"},{"type":"text","value":" to start your server and navigate to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://localhost:3000"},{"type":"text","value":" to see your route in action."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want to deploy your application? Check out the "},{"type":"link","href":"./guide/hosting.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hosting guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"typescript-configuration","text":"TypeScript Configuration","level":2},{"id":"install-dependencies","text":"Install Dependencies","level":2},{"id":"update-configuration-files","text":"Update Configuration Files","level":2},{"id":"add-the-basic-templating","text":"Add the Basic Templating","level":2},{"id":"the-router-configuration","text":"The Router Configuration","level":2},{"id":"the-root-of-your-application","text":"The Root of Your Application","level":2},{"id":"writing-your-first-route","text":"Writing Your First Route","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> [!NOTE]\n> If you already created a project with the CLI or by cloning an example from the [Getting Started](./getting-started) guide, you can skip this guide and move on to the [Routing](./guide/routing) guide.\n\n_So you want to build a TanStack Start project from scratch?_\n\nThis guide will help you build a **very** basic TanStack Start web application. Together, we will use TanStack Start to:\n\n- Serve an index page\n- Display a counter\n- Increment the counter on the server and client\n\n[Here is what that will look like](https://stackblitz.com/github/tanstack/router/tree/main/examples/react/start-counter)\n\nLet's create a new project directory and initialize it.\n\n```shell\nmkdir myApp\ncd myApp\nnpm init -y\n```\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> We use `npm` in all of these examples, but you can use your package manager of choice instead.\n\n## TypeScript Configuration\n\nWe highly recommend using TypeScript with TanStack Start. Create a `tsconfig.json` file with at least the following settings:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"Bundler\",\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"strictNullChecks\": true\n  }\n}\n```\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Enabling `verbatimModuleSyntax` can result in server bundles leaking into client bundles. It is recommended to keep this option disabled.\n\n## Install Dependencies\n\nTanStack Start is powered by [TanStack Router](https://tanstack.com/router) and supports [Vite](https://vite.dev/) or [Rsbuild](https://rsbuild.dev/) as the build tool.\n\nTo install Start and Router, run:\n\n```shell\nnpm i @tanstack/react-start @tanstack/react-router\n```\n\nYou'll also need React:\n\n```shell\nnpm i react react-dom\n```\n\nInstall the build tool and React integration you want to use:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```shell\nnpm i -D vite @vitejs/plugin-react\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```shell\nnpm i -D @rsbuild/core @rsbuild/plugin-react\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nIf you use Vite, you can also use `@vitejs/plugin-react-swc` instead of `@vitejs/plugin-react`.\n\nand some TypeScript:\n\n```shell\nnpm i -D typescript @types/react @types/react-dom @types/node\n```\n\n## Update Configuration Files\n\nWe'll then update our `package.json` to use your build tool's CLI and set `\"type\": \"module\"`:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```json\n{\n  // ...\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite dev\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```json\n{\n  // ...\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"rsbuild dev\",\n    \"build\": \"rsbuild build\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThen configure TanStack Start's build tool plugin:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```ts title=\"vite.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\nimport viteReact from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  server: {\n    port: 3000,\n  },\n  resolve: {\n    tsconfigPaths: true,\n  },\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart(),\n    // react's vite plugin must come after start's vite plugin\n    viteReact(),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```ts title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { pluginReact } from '@rsbuild/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  server: {\n    port: 3000,\n  },\n  plugins: [pluginReact(), tanstackStart()],\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Add the Basic Templating\n\nThere are 2 required files for TanStack Start usage:\n\n1. The router configuration\n2. The root of your application\n\nOnce configuration is done, we'll have a file tree that looks like the following:\n\n```\n.\n├── src/\n│   ├── routes/\n│   │   └── `__root.tsx`\n│   ├── `router.tsx`\n│   ├── `routeTree.gen.ts`\n├── `vite.config.ts` or `rsbuild.config.ts`\n├── `package.json`\n└── `tsconfig.json`\n```\n\n## The Router Configuration\n\nThis is the file that will dictate the behavior of TanStack Router used within Start. Here, you can configure everything\nfrom the default [preloading functionality](/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/preloading) to [caching staleness](/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/data-loading).\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> You won't have a `routeTree.gen.ts` file yet. This file will be generated when you run TanStack Start for the first time.\n\n```tsx\n// src/router.tsx\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nexport function getRouter() {\n  const router = createRouter({\n    routeTree,\n    scrollRestoration: true,\n  })\n\n  return router\n}\n```\n\n## The Root of Your Application\n\nFinally, we need to create the root of our application. This is the entry point for all other routes. The code in this file will wrap all other routes in the application.\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/__root.tsx\nimport type { ReactNode } from 'react'\nimport {\n  Outlet,\n  createRootRoute,\n  HeadContent,\n  Scripts,\n} from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  head: () => ({\n    meta: [\n      {\n        charSet: 'utf-8',\n      },\n      {\n        name: 'viewport',\n        content: 'width=device-width, initial-scale=1',\n      },\n      {\n        title: 'TanStack Start Starter',\n      },\n    ],\n  }),\n  component: RootComponent,\n})\n\nfunction RootComponent() {\n  return (\n    <RootDocument>\n      <Outlet />\n    </RootDocument>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction RootDocument({ children }: Readonly<{ children: ReactNode }>) {\n  return (\n    <html>\n      <head>\n        <HeadContent />\n      </head>\n      <body>\n        {children}\n        <Scripts />\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Writing Your First Route\n\nNow that we have the basic templating setup, we can write our first route. This is done by creating a new file in the `src/routes` directory.\n\n```tsx\n// src/routes/index.tsx\nimport * as fs from 'node:fs'\nimport { createFileRoute, useRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nconst filePath = 'count.txt'\n\nasync function readCount() {\n  return parseInt(\n    await fs.promises.readFile(filePath, 'utf-8').catch(() => '0'),\n  )\n}\n\nconst getCount = createServerFn({\n  method: 'GET',\n}).handler(() => {\n  return readCount()\n})\n\nconst updateCount = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .validator((d: number) => d)\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    const count = await readCount()\n    await fs.promises.writeFile(filePath, `${count + data}`)\n  })\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  component: Home,\n  loader: async () => await getCount(),\n})\n\nfunction Home() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const state = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      onClick={() => {\n        updateCount({ data: 1 }).then(() => {\n          router.invalidate()\n        })\n      }}\n    >\n      Add 1 to {state}?\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThat's it! 🤯 You've now set up a TanStack Start project and written your first route. 🎉\n\nYou can now run `npm run dev` to start your server and navigate to `http://localhost:3000` to see your route in action.\n\nYou want to deploy your application? Check out the [hosting guide](./guide/hosting.md).\n"}
